{"url": "https://grad.umn.edu/admissions/application-instructions/application-fees/gsdo-application-fee-waiver", "final_url": "https://grad.umn.edu/admissions/application-instructions/application-fees/gsdo-application-fee-waiver", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-12", "text": "Close submenu\nApplication Fees\nBig 10 Academic Alliance Fee Waiver Program\nSkip to main content\nGo to the University of Minnesota System home page\nCrookston Duluth Morris Rochester Twin Cities\nOne Stop MyU\nSearch\n\u00d7\nGraduate School\nApply\nSearch\nAbout\n\u00bb\nAcademic & Career Support\n\u00bb\nAdmissions\n\u00bb\nGraduate Programs\n\u00bb\nFunding\n\u00bb\nDiversity\n\u00bb\nNews & Events\n\u00bb\nBreadcrumb\nGraduate School Admissions Application Instructions Application Fees GSDO Application Fee Waiver\nGSDO Application Fee Waiver\nMain menu\nAdmissions\nApplication Instructions\nExpand Application Instructions menu\nDeadlines\nApplication Fees\nExpand Application Fees menu\nBig 10 Academic Alliance Fee Waiver Program\nGRE\nOfficial Transcripts & Credentials\nUnofficial Transcripts & Credentials\nRecommendation Letters\nInternational Student Resources\nChange or Add a Degree Objective\nReadmission\nThe Graduate School Diversity Office (GSDO) fee waiver program opens on September 7, 2026.\nYou may be eligible for a GSDO application fee waiver when you apply for admission to a research-based PhD or master's program at the University of Minnesota. Please carefully read the information below and follow the instructions provided. Contact the Graduate School Diversity Office (gsdorecruit@umn.edu) if you have questions.\nEligible Fee Waiver Programs\nThe Graduate School Diversity Office is responsible only for application fee waivers to research-based PhD and master\u2019s programs. We are unable to provide waivers to those who are submitting applications outside of our standard application processing system (Slate), or to those applying to the following programs/colleges: Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS); Doctor of Juridical Science (SJD); Doctor of Medicine (MD); Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD); Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM); Juris Doctor (JD); Master of Laws (Business Law LL.M; general LL.M); Master of Medical Laboratory Sciences (MMLS); Master of Occupational Therapy (MOT); Medical Scientist Training Program (MSTP; MD/PhD); Minnesota Carlson; and School of Public Health programs.\nEligibility Criteria\nApplicants requesting a fee waiver from the University of Minnesota\u2019s Graduate School Diversity Office must meet the following criteria to receive consideration:\nBe a U.S. citizen or permanent resident\nBe seeking to obtain a graduate degree for the first time (current graduate students, those who are seeking a second graduate degree, and those who have already earned a terminal degree are not eligible)\nMeet at least ONE of the following:\nParticipated in a graduate school preparation program: Must have participated in a program directed by a program leader that prepares students to earn an advanced degree and pursue an academic and/or research career.\nSubmitted an inquiry at a UMN graduate school recruitment event: Must have visited the GSDO recruiter/booth at a recruitment conference/event and completed our GSDO inquiry form.\nSteps to obtain an application fee waiver:\nStart an online application, but do not submit the application until you have received confirmation that the application fee has been waived.\nSend the GSDO an email (gsdorecruit@umn.edu) with the subject Application Fee Waiver.\nAttached to or included in the email must be proof of participation/membership in a program/organization (typically a letter from the program/organization director, documentation, verification form, etc.) or the recruitment event at which you completed a GSDO inquiry form.\nThe GSDO will send verification via email of the applied waiver or may request additional documentation/proof, if needed.\nThe applicant can submit their application without paying the fee once an email receipt has been sent stating that the application fee has been waived.\nImportant Information and Reminders for Fall 2026 Applicants\nThe application fee waiver request window for Fall 2026 will open on Monday, September 7, 2026, and will run until Friday, December 4, 2026, at Noon CST, or until fund capacity is reached (whichever occurs first).\nPlease start your application early, as we will be unable to accommodate requests that fall close to the deadline.\nBig Ten Academic Alliance FreeApp Program\nAs a member of the Big Ten, the University of Minnesota\u2019s Graduate School participates in the Big Ten Academic Alliance (BTAA) FreeApp Program. The program is designed to increase access to graduate education for domestic students. The GSDO is automatically notified of all applicants who complete a FreeApp request and will email those applicants regarding next steps. FreeApp applicants will need to meet the eligibility criteria listed above to be considered for a GSDO application fee waiver.\nQuestions about the fee waiver program can be directed to gsdorecruit@umn.edu.\nView GSDO Statement of Nondiscrimination\nGraduate School Footer\nPrivacy Policy\nSite Map\nStaff Directory\nOffice Locations\nResources For\nProspective Graduate Students\nCurrent Graduate Students\nPostdoctoral Scholars\nFaculty & Staff\n\u00a9 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota. All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Privacy Statement\nReport Web Accessibility Issues", "links": [["", "https://grad.umn.edu/admissions/application-instructions/application-fees/gsdo-application-fee-waiver#mm-0"], ["About", "https://grad.umn.edu/about"], ["Open submenu", "https://grad.umn.edu/admissions/application-instructions/application-fees/gsdo-application-fee-waiver#mm-2"], ["Academic & Career Support", "https://grad.umn.edu/academic-career-support"], ["Open submenu", "https://grad.umn.